meta {
  name: Delete Document
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires ANY of `business_admin:document_management__delete_document`, `branch_admin:document_management__delete_document` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission` / `@RequireAnyPermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Soft-delete a document (sets `deletedAt`). It drops out of List/Get, but its
  version snapshots are PRESERVED in the database for the record. 404
  `DOCUMENT_NOT_FOUND` if already missing.
}
